       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.          TIRWSMOD.
       AUTHOR.              C HILLES.
       DATE-WRITTEN.        9/1/83.
       DATE-COMPILED.
      *INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
      *SECURITY.
      *REMARKS.     ISSUE AND RETURN WORKSHEET MODIFY PROGRAM.
      *
      *    ON NOVEMBER 30, 1983, CHANGED PARAMETERS FOR CALL TO
      *    "TSPLPRT".  NOW RETURNS ENTIRE SPOOLER REC, BUT NO
      *    MESSAGE BUFFER.  CIH.
      *
      *    ON APRIL 26, 1984, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
      *    1. CHANGED PARAMETERS TO INCLUDE ENTIRE
      *       SPOOLER REC (USER, ACCOUNT, TERM NUMBER, AND ALL 5 SPOOLER
      *       NUMBERS), RATHER THAN JUST SPOOL-PRT.  THIS IS BECAUSE THE
      *       5TH SPOOLER NUMBER WAS USED TO DETERMINE WHETHER HALF-SHEE
      *       PAPER WAS BEING USED, BUT THIS KEY WAS LOST WHEN GOING
      *       BETWEEN SUB-PROGRAMS.  CIH.
      *
      *    2.  CHANGED THE "DWLITEM-LIST" (DATA ITEM LIST
      *    FOR DWLITEM SEGMENT) TO "ALL-ITEMS" (PULL OUT ALL ITEMS
      *    IN DATA SET).  THIS IS BECAUSE THE TEST DATABASE HAD A
      *    DATA ITEM CHANGED IN DWLITEM, BUT IT WAS NOT CHANGED AT ALL
      *    PLANTS (YET).  CIH.
      *
      *    ON OCT 8, 1984, CHANGED THIS SUBPROGRAM TO WORK FOR BOTH
      *    THE AKRON PLANTS AND THE SUB-PLANTS.  FORMERLY THERE WAS
      *    A SEPERATE VERSION OF ALL THE STORES PROGRAMS FOR AKRON
      *    PLANTS.  THIS INVOLVED THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
      *        1.  THE "DEFAULT EXPENSE CLASS" LOGIC WAS MOVED FROM
      *            THIS SUBPROGRAM INTO THE "TIREDIT" EDITING SUB-
      *            PROGRAM.  THIS REQUIRED ADDING THE "STR-EXPENSE-CLASS
      *            AS A PARAMETER TO THE CALL OF "TIREDIT".
      *            (DEFAULT EXP CLASS IS NOT USED IN AKRON, AND THE
      *            EDITING SUB-PROGRAM WILL HANDLE THESE DIFFERENCES).
      *
      *        2.  THE "TIREDIT", "TQTYEDIT", "TWSPRT" SUBPROGRAMS WERE
      *            CHANGED WITH SPECIAL LOGIC FOR AKRON.
      *
      *        3.  A DIFFERENT FORMS FILE IS MAINTAINED FOR AKRON AND TH
      *            PLANTS.  THE AKRON VERSION HAS A "WORK CENTER" FIELD.
      *            THE PLANT VERSION HAS THIS FIELD, BUT IT IS DISPLAY
      *            ONLY, NO ENHANCEMENTS (INVISIBLE).  (THUS THE SCREEN
      *            BUFFER IS THE SAME IN THE PROGRAM).  THE AKRON VERSIO
      *            HAS A 1 BYTE "CHARGE TYPE FIELD".  THE PLANTS VERSION
      *            HAS A 2 BYTE EXTENSION TO THE CHARGE DEPT.  SO ON
      *            THE AKRON FORM FILE, THE SECOND HALF THE THIS EXTENSI
      *            FIELD WAS CHANGED TO  DISPLAY ONLY, NO ENHANCEMENTS.
      *            (ONCE AGAIN, SO THAT THE SCREEN BUFFER DOES NOT NEED
      *            TO BE DIFFERENT FOR THE TWO VERSIONS).
      *             CIH.
      *
      *    ON JANUARY 23, 1985, CHANGED THE "K-TERMINAL" PARAMETER
      *    (THE TERMINAL NUMBER OBTAINED FROM "TSPLPRT", WHICH IS PASSED
      *    BACK AND FORTH TO "TIRMAIN") FROM 9(2) TO 9(4).  CIH.
      *
      *    ON JUNE 26, 1985, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
      *      1.  ALLOWED THE USER TO MODIFY THE CORPORATE CODE ON THE
      *          WORKSHEET.
      *      2.  ADDED A DELETE WORKSHEET OPTION TO THE FIRST SCREEN.
      *          THIS DELETE IS ACCOMPLISHED BY A CALL TO A NEW
      *          SUBPROGRAM "TIRWSDLT".
      *      3.  ADDED A CALL TO "TSHWRDFM" TO DO THE SHOWFORM,
      *          READFIELDS, FIELDEDITS, AND SPECIAL FUNCTION KEYS.
      *          CIH.
      *
      *   10/09/85  ADDED CALLS TO FINDJCW, NLAPPEND, CATOPEN, AND
      *             CATCLOSE IN ORDER TO ACCOMODATE THE NATIVE
      *             LANGUAGE SUPPORT FACILITY.  ADDED LINKAGES AND
      *             ALSO MADE THE CHANGE TO THE FORMFILE NAMES.
      *   10/09/85  CHANGED ALL REFERENCES OF TSCRPRNT TO TSCRPRT2,
      *             TDATECHK TO TDATECK2.
      *             THIS WAS TO INCORPORATE THE NATIVE LANGUAGE
      *             SUPPORT VERSIONS OF THESE SUBROUTINES.
      *                             -TW COTTON.
      *
      *   12/1/85   CHANGED TO FIX SMALL PROBLEM CAUSED BY ABOVE
      *             LANGUAGE CHANGE.  THE PROGRAM SKIPPED THE ERROR
      *             "QUANTITY MUST BE ENTERED" RETURNED BY "TQTYEDIT".
      *             HOWEVER AFTER CONVERSION TO ERROR CATALOG, THE
      *             MESSAGE BECAME "Q19: QUANTITY IS A REQUIRED FIELD".
      *             THIS CAUSED A ZERO QUANTITY TO BE DISALLOWED (SHOULD
      *             BE ALLOWED SO QUANTITIES CAN BE ZEROED OUT ON
      *             WORKSHEET).  FIXED THIS PROBLEM.  CIH.
      *
      *    06/17/86.
      *      REPLACED CALL TO "TFDESC" WITH CALL TO "CDESC".  "CDESC"
      *      HAS MORE OPTIONS, AND HANDLES THE DATA SETS "DMANPART" - US
      *      THE MANUFACTURER ENTRIES AS PART OF DESCRIPTION. CIH.
      *
      *C
      *C   03NOV1994    WILL MCINTYRE   REQUEST 94-027
      *C     ADDED CODE TO PASS NEW PARMS TO TQTYEDIT, TO CHECK FOR LIMITS
      *C     ON STOREROOM RETURNS.
018200*C
      *C   MAY 31, 1995  JEFF BUNGO     REQUEST #94-058
      *C     ADDED PARAMETERS TO CALL OF TQTYEDIT TO WRITE TO MSTRWITH
      *C     IN CASE WITHDRAWAL HAS INSUFFICIENT ON HAND.
      *C
      *C  06/12/96    JEFF BUNGO
      *C     EXPAND DATE FIELDS FOR YEAR 2000 COMPLIANCE.
      *C     RECOMPILE TO PICK UP NEW FILE FORMATS.
      *C
      *C  05/07/97    JEFF BUNGO
      *C     INCLUDE NEW PARMETERS ON CALL TO TQTYEDIT
      *C     CODE OWNER, BIN OWNERS, AND FRANCHISE TABLE.
      *C     TQTYEDIT WILL FORCE WITHDRAWAL FROM GOODYEAR
      *C     OWNED BINS BEFORE WITHDRAWALING FROM FRANCHISE
      *C     OWNED BINS.
      *C
      *C  09/17/97    JEFF BUNGO
      *C     AKRON RESEARCH (119) ONLY.
      *C     IF RESEARCH AND MAJ/SUB GROUP IS 2890, THEN DISPLAY
      *C     ENTERED CCS DATA FOR THE WORKSHEET AND CODE AND ALLOW
      *C     MODIFICATION.  IF THE QUANTITY IS DECREASED, THEN THE
      *C     LAST RECORDS (UP TO THE DECREASED QUANTITY) OF THE
      *C     WORKSHEET AND CODE WILL BE DELETED.  IF THE QUANTITY
      *C     IS INCREASED, THEN ADDITIONAL RECORDS WILL BE OPENED
      *C     FOR INPUT.
      *C
      *C   OCTOBER 1995  JIM COFFMAN
      *C     CHANGED ISSPARTS PARAMETERS TO BE INCLUDED IN A COPYLIB
      *C     MEMBER. THIS WAS NECESSARY TO ALLOW THE AREA TO BE
      *C     EXPANDABLE TO CONTAIN THE LINK TO A WORK ORDER LOGIC
      *C     REQUEST NOW AVAILABLE IN AN E1 REQUISITION CREATE.
      *C
      *C   11/21/97      JEFF BUNGO
      *C     FOR AKRON RESEARCH (119) ONLY.
      *C     EXPAND THE CODES FOR CCS LOCATION TRACKING BEYOND
      *C     MAJ/SUB GROUP 2890.  READ IN DATA AREA THAT WILL
      *C     CONTAIN TABLE OF ADDITIONAL CODES TO BE TRACKED.
      *C     IF CODE ON WORKSHEET IS IN THE TABLE THEN FORCE
      *C     ENTRY OF CCS DATA.  THE DATA AREA CONTAINING THE
      *C     CCS CODES IS "CCSCODES".  CHANGE THIS DATA AREA
      *C     TO ADD OR REMOVE CCS CODES ACCORDING TO THE TABLE
      *C     DEFINITION IN WORKING STORAGE.  THE DATA AREA FORCES
      *C     A MAXIMUM OF 250 ENTRIES (8 * 250 = 2000).
      *C
017300*C
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
       COPY SPECIALN IN COPYLIB.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT MSTORERM-CD-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0201
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MWRKLIST-WK-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0301
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DWLITEM-WK-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1501
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                     WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DCCSDATA
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS6601
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                     WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MPLTINFO
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0501
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                 ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DISPLAY-FILE
                  ASSIGN TO WORKSTATION-ZUDCSTR-SI
                  ORGANIZATION IS TRANSACTION
                  ACCESS IS DYNAMIC
                  RELATIVE KEY IS SFL-PTR
                  FILE STATUS IS DISPLAY-STATUS
                  CONTROL-AREA IS WS-CONTROL.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.

      *------ FD STATEMENT AREA FOR IBM ONLY ------*
       FD  MWRKLIST-WK-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MWRKLIST-WK-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0300  OF MCFLCS0301.

       FD  MSTORERM-CD-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MSTORERM-CD-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0200  OF MCFLCS0201.

       FD  DWLITEM-WK-O
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DWLITEM-WK-REC-O.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS1500  OF MCFLCS1501.

       FD  DCCSDATA
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DCCSDATA-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS6600  OF MCFLCS6601.

       FD  MPLTINFO
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MPLTINFO-REC.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0500 OF MCFLCS0501.
019200
       FD  DISPLAY-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED.
       01  DISPLAY-REC                   PIC X(1500).
      *------ FD STATEMENT AREA FOR IBM ONLY ------*

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.

       77  SUB                           PIC 9(2)  VALUE 0.
       77  SUB2                          PIC 9(2)  VALUE 0.
       77  SUB3                          PIC S9(4) BINARY VALUE 0.
       77  SUB5                          PIC 9(2)  VALUE 0.
       77  TABLE-LIMIT                   PIC 9(2)  VALUE 0.
       77  CHANGE-FLAG                   PIC X(1)  VALUE "N".
       77  DUP-FLAG                      PIC X(1)  VALUE "N".
       77  HANDLE-BLOWUP-FLAG            PIC X VALUE "Y".
       77  ENTRY-ERROR                   PIC X VALUE "N".
       COPY FUNCTDEF IN COPYLIB.

